                    insight_durable:        `Durable network advantage: you turned position into appropriable rent. Centrality and appropriation rose together and trust held — the rent accrues to Anatolia, not just the ecosystem, and is hard to copy because it's positional, not a product.`,
                    insight_notcaptured:    `You built a strong position but left the rent on the table. High centrality with low appropriation means the network creates value that flows to your partners — you needed exclusivity clauses, embedded standards and switching costs to make it yours.`,
                    insight_short:          `You fell short of a durable broker position. Without occupying the structural holes and concentrating a focused portfolio, Anatolia drifts back toward a commodity component supplier — margins compressing toward 6–7%.`,
                    insight_straddle:       `You straddled the GeoNorth–AtlasMap conflicting tie at some point — and it cost you in trust and retaliation. The conflicting tie cannot be kept cost-free; committing to one would have built a more defensible position.`,
                    insight_disinter:       `You broadcast your brokerage and were disintermediated — partners you introduced now meet without you. Visible brokerage has a two-quarter shelf life; durable rent needs structural lock-in, not a press release.`,
                    insight_leak:           `You leaked your sensor-fusion roadmap to win an innovation tie that fed a rival. Innovation access is valuable, but unbounded disclosure erodes the very advantage you were trying to build.`,
                    insight_overcommit:     `You resourced more positions than your engineering attention can carry — co-developments slipped and delivery degraded. Portfolio shape beats portfolio size under a hard attention cap.`,
                    insight_lasts:          `This is an advantage that lasts: a focused, well-governed portfolio with embedded lock-in and a real feedback rule. As the network matures, the rent keeps accruing to Anatolia.`,

                    hint_straddle:          `You're straddling the conflicting tie — trust is bleeding and retaliation is coming. Commit to GeoNorth or AtlasMap and re-confirm the choice; you cannot keep both cost-free.`,
